<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico to drain 1.999 bln pesos.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico to drain 1.999 bln pesos.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico sought to drain 1.999 billion pesos from the secondary market on Friday through a combination of three direct sales of paper and four repurchase agreements, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were offered or assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    349 days   20.86 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    181 days</p>
<p>    150 million     90 days</p>
<p>The amounts and maturities of the repurchase agreements were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    400 million     46 days</p>
<p>    700 million     38 days</p>
<p>    300 million	6 days</p>
<p>    149 million	3 days</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
